  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The strength of the sale & purchase market persists, although the freight market experienced \na minor correction, with the Baltic Dry Index decreasing to 2991 points today, down from 3151 points \nrecorded last Friday, driven by reduced Capesize and Panamax spot rates. \n \nSecondhand vessel prices remain near multi-year highs, as shipowners continue to maintain healthy \nbuying appetite, having recorded an impressive tally of 20 transactions this week: 1 caper, 4 x post- \npanamaxes, 3 x kamsarmaxes, 1 panamax, 2 x ultramaxes, 4 x supramaxes and 5 x handysizes.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain weak overall, with the exception of Pakistan. Pakistan's \nmarket is firm as it depends on recycled steel due to import restrictions caused by the ongoing conflict. \nFor an overview of demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
